  "construction_knowledge": "CC0",
  "notes": "Zoo 0.91.0. A 1970s-1990s floor-standing pull-knob cigarette machine on splayed legs: chrome frame and top trim, a brass strip and key lock, woodgrain sides, a header ad lit faintly (M_CigMachine_<art>_Face, Lux's power cut takes it), two rows of packs over the minors notice, a pull knob per column in chrome or amber, a coin slot and return, a delivery tray. Planned and painted in core/cigarette_forms.py. Every brand is INVENTED (core/cigarette_brands.py) and no pack is a real pack's trade dress; the Surgeon General's warning is the statutory text. Lettering is Pixel Operator, CC0, via Pixelcoat. The back is the slot's +Y face; collision is the cabinet box."
